<p>If you cannot approve right away, Duet does not stall. It finishes the parts that need no approval and brings the request back later. Results cite the email, file or spreadsheet they came from. Every action also passes Anthropic's <strong>auto mode classifier</strong>, the same safeguard that stops Claude Code from taking steps you did not ask for. How that classifier became the default is covered in this wiki's <a href="#!news-20260814-auto-mode-stateless-mcp">Defaults That Stop Asking</a>.</p>
<p>The right-hand tier matters because an approval button is not the last line of defense. Tired or busy people approve out of habit. Trading securities and moving money between accounts are where that habit ends most expensively, so Duet never puts up an approval screen for them at all.</p>

