<ul>
    <li><strong>A proxy holds the credentials.</strong> Duet handles credentials the way Claude Managed Agents do. Sign-in data is kept apart from the environment where the model runs code, and a separate proxy fetches the credentials and makes the API calls. When a password has to be typed, it goes into a separate form, not the chat.</li>
    <li><strong>A classifier reads every outgoing message.</strong> A new dedicated classifier and a safety system prompt check each message. The strictest tier, such as credit card numbers and government ID numbers, is refused even on request. Health and personal finance details go out only when you explicitly tell Duet to send them.</li>
    <li><strong>Payments use a one-time card.</strong> Purchases go through Link, Stripe's digital wallet. Duet confirms the item, Link asks for your approval again, and then a virtual card valid for that one purchase is created. Your real card number never reaches the store. Shop Pay works at Shopify stores.</li>
</ul>
<p>Defenses against <strong>prompt injection</strong>, instructions hidden in a web page to steer an agent, come from Anthropic's browser-use research. Internal red teams and an outside firm penetration-tested Duet, and it is covered by the public bug bounty. Anthropic says it will publish more safety design detail in the coming days.</p>

